      90 PSI to <strong>93 PSI</strong> to give a comfortable margin. Aerogel wrap is mandatory — it drops heat loss
      from ~180W to ~20W over the run, preventing steam quality degradation and water hammer from condensate slugging.
      Locomotive comparison: a standard steam locomotive carries steam 8–12 feet at 160–250 PSI with similar bore —
      our lower working pressure makes the ¾" bore even more appropriate for our scale.
