      <h3>Cold is manageable — moisture is the enemy</h3>
      <p>The biggest arctic risks are brake line moisture freezing and battery cold-soak capacity loss. The boiler takes longer to heat up from frozen, but the steam system itself is inherently more cold-tolerant than an ICE — no oil-thickening engine drag, no fuel-line freezing, no glow plug issues.</p>
